-- 22 September 2026 daily current-affairs desk: eight original, official-source-verified briefs.
insert into public.current_affairs_briefs (slug, published_on, title, summary, why_it_matters, background, source_title, source_url, source_publisher, source_published_on, prelims_takeaways, quick_check, visual_data, status, reviewed_at) values
(
$$2026-09-22-national-accounts-sources-methods$$,$$2026-09-22$$,$$MoSPI publishes sources and methods for the 2022–23 National Accounts series$$,
$$MoSPI released “Sources and Methods for Compilation of National Accounts Statistics,” documenting concepts, definitions, data sources and compilation practices for the National Accounts series with base year 2022–23.$$,
$$This is a statistical-methodology release. It helps distinguish a base-year revision from a fresh economic policy measure, and makes the official compilation framework available for scrutiny and study.$$,
$$The 2022–23 series replaced the 2011–12 series and is described by MoSPI as the eighth base-year revision of National Accounts Statistics. The series was later updated to incorporate changes associated with the new PPI and IIP series.$$,
$$Sources and Methods for Compilation of National Accounts Statistics$$,$$https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2313018&lang=1&reg=48$$,$$Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation / Press Information Bureau$$,$$2026-09-21$$,
$$["The National Accounts base year is 2022–23.","It replaced the earlier 2011–12 series.","MoSPI calls this the eighth base-year revision of National Accounts Statistics.","The publication documents concepts, definitions, sources and methods."]$$::jsonb,
$$[{"question":"What is the base year of the new National Accounts series?","answer":"2022–23."},{"question":"Does the methods publication itself announce a new fiscal policy?","answer":"No. It documents the statistical compilation framework."}]$$::jsonb,
$${"title":"National Accounts revision","steps":["A new base year is selected.","Sources and methods are defined.","Official estimates are compiled and updated.","A methods publication explains the framework."]}$$::jsonb,$$published$$,now()
),
(
$$2026-09-22-india-new-zealand-fta-entry-into-force$$,$$2026-09-22$$,$$India–New Zealand FTA gets a confirmed entry-into-force date$$,
$$India and New Zealand announced that their Free Trade Agreement will enter into force on 20 October 2026 after completion of the required internal processes.$$,
$$This completes a key treaty-implementation step. Signing, domestic implementation and entry into force are distinct stages; the date is more precise than the earlier report of New Zealand’s enabling legislation.$$,
$$The FTA was signed on 27 April 2026 at Bharat Mandapam, New Delhi. The release states that India will receive zero-duty access for 100% of its exports to New Zealand from day one of entry into force.$$,
$$India-New Zealand FTA to Enter into Force from 20 October 2026$$,$$https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2313143&lang=1&reg=1$$,$$Ministry of Commerce and Industry / Press Information Bureau$$,$$2026-09-21$$,
$$["The FTA is scheduled to enter into force on 20 October 2026.","It was signed on 27 April 2026 in New Delhi.","The stated access for Indian exports is zero duty on 100% of exports to New Zealand from day one.","Entry into force follows completion of internal processes."]$$::jsonb,
$$[{"question":"When is the India–New Zealand FTA scheduled to enter into force?","answer":"20 October 2026."},{"question":"Is treaty signature the same as entry into force?","answer":"No. Internal processes must also be completed."}]$$::jsonb,
$${"title":"FTA implementation sequence","steps":["Countries sign the agreement.","They complete domestic procedures.","They confirm entry-into-force requirements.","Treaty commitments become operational."]}$$::jsonb,$$published$$,now()
),
(
$$2026-09-22-critical-mineral-recycling-concept-paper$$,$$2026-09-22$$,$$Ministry of Mines launches a concept paper on critical-mineral recycling$$,
$$The Ministry of Mines launched a Concept Paper on the Critical Mineral Recycling Ecosystem at a national seminar on circular economy. It frames recovery from end-of-life products and secondary sources as part of resource efficiency and domestic capability.$$,
$$Critical-mineral security is linked to clean-energy technologies, electronics, defence and advanced manufacturing. A concept paper is a strategic framework, not by itself a binding recycling regulation or a mining licence.$$,
$$The release identifies e-waste, industrial waste and other end-of-life materials as secondary sources. Technical sessions covered lithium-ion battery metal recovery, black-mass processing, e-waste collection and non-ferrous-metal recycling.$$,
$$Union Minister Calls for Stronger Recycling, Innovation and Jan Bhagidari for Critical Minerals Security$$,$$https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2313165&lang=2&reg=48$$,$$Ministry of Mines / Press Information Bureau$$,$$2026-09-21$$,
$$["The Ministry launched a Concept Paper on the Critical Mineral Recycling Ecosystem.","End-of-life products can be secondary sources of critical minerals.","Critical-mineral recycling supports a circular economy and resource efficiency.","The release highlights lithium-ion battery recovery and black-mass processing."]$$::jsonb,
$$[{"question":"What are end-of-life products in this context?","answer":"Secondary sources from which critical minerals can be recovered."},{"question":"Does a concept paper itself create a binding mining licence?","answer":"No. It is a strategic framework."}]$$::jsonb,
$${"title":"Critical-mineral circularity","steps":["Products reach end of life.","E-waste and scrap enter formal collection.","Materials are processed and minerals recovered.","Recovered inputs reduce dependence on primary sources."]}$$::jsonb,$$published$$,now()
),
(
$$2026-09-22-sowa-rigpa-pharmacopoeia-working-group$$,$$2026-09-22$$,$$Sowa-Rigpa working group begins pharmacopoeia and formulary standardisation$$,
$$The first Sowa-Rigpa Working Group meeting under the Pharmacopoeia Commission for Indian Medicine and Homoeopathy was held in Ghaziabad to begin development of Sowa-Rigpa pharmacopoeias and formularies.$$,
$$This is a traditional-medicine quality-standardisation development. It concerns regulatory and quality-assurance documents, rather than an endorsement of every product or practice marketed as traditional medicine.$$,
$$PCIM&H is a subordinate office under the Ministry of Ayush. The work is to proceed under the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940 and associated Rules, supporting quality standards for Sowa-Rigpa drugs.$$,
$$Sowa-Rigpa Working Group Holds First Meeting Under PCIM&H$$,$$https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2313118&lang=2&reg=48$$,$$Ministry of Ayush / Press Information Bureau$$,$$2026-09-21$$,
$$["The working group is under PCIM&H.","It is developing Sowa-Rigpa pharmacopoeias and formularies.","PCIM&H is a subordinate office of the Ministry of Ayush.","The work is within the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940 framework."]$$::jsonb,
$$[{"question":"Which body hosts the Sowa-Rigpa Working Group?","answer":"The Pharmacopoeia Commission for Indian Medicine and Homoeopathy."},{"question":"What is the group developing?","answer":"Sowa-Rigpa pharmacopoeias and formularies."}]$$::jsonb,
$${"title":"Traditional-medicine quality framework","steps":["Experts identify standards requirements.","Pharmacopoeias specify recognised quality benchmarks.","Formularies organise preparations and references.","Regulatory quality assurance supports safer use."]}$$::jsonb,$$published$$,now()
),
(
$$2026-09-22-nal-jal-mitra-jjm2-skilling$$,$$2026-09-22$$,$$Nal Jal Mitra framework advances skilled rural-water operations under JJM 2.0$$,
$$At a national virtual conference, the Department of Drinking Water and Sanitation asked States and UTs to accelerate Nal Jal Mitra and Sujalam Shakti initiatives for operation, maintenance and water-quality surveillance under Jal Jeevan Mission 2.0.$$,
$$The item shifts attention from infrastructure creation to sustainable service delivery. A trained local workforce supports the functioning of rural piped-water systems; it is not a replacement for the mission’s physical infrastructure or public-health standards.$$,
$$DDWS, the Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship, and NCVTE developed an NSQF-aligned Nal Jal Mitra qualification. States and State Water and Sanitation Missions were asked to decide by 15 October whether to adopt the existing course or develop a State-specific course.$$,
$$DDWS Organised First Virtual Conference on Strengthening Skilled Rural Water Workforce Under Jal Jeevan Mission 2.0$$,$$https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2313201&lang=2&reg=48$$,$$Department of Drinking Water and Sanitation / Press Information Bureau$$,$$2026-09-21$$,
$$["Nal Jal Mitra is an NSQF-aligned rural-water skilling qualification.","It supports operation, maintenance and first-level repairs of rural water systems.","DDWS developed it with MSDE and NCVTE.","States were asked to decide on course adoption or a State-specific course by 15 October 2026."]$$::jsonb,
$$[{"question":"What does Nal Jal Mitra principally support?","answer":"Skilled operation and maintenance of rural water-supply systems."},{"question":"Which framework aligns the qualification?","answer":"The National Skills Qualifications Framework (NSQF)."}]$$::jsonb,
$${"title":"Rural-water service workforce","steps":["Water infrastructure is created.","States assess local workforce needs.","Nal Jal Mitras receive relevant skills.","Operators maintain systems and support water-quality surveillance."]}$$::jsonb,$$published$$,now()
),
(
$$2026-09-22-legacy-dumpsite-transformation$$,$$2026-09-22$$,$$SBM-U 2.0 frames legacy-dumpsite remediation as urban land recovery$$,
$$A PIB backgrounder explains how cities under Swachh Bharat Mission-Urban 2.0 are transforming legacy dumpsites into environmentally sustainable and productive spaces. It cites processing of about 62,252 metric tonnes of waste and reclamation of nearly 22 acres at Bhalswa.$$,
$$Legacy-waste remediation joins urban sanitation, circular economy and land-use governance. A backgrounder explains programme context and examples; it is not a nationwide notification of identical completion outcomes for every city.$$,
$$SBM-U began in October 2014 and SBM-U 2.0 in October 2021. Legacy dumpsites contain accumulated municipal waste, so remediation may involve processing, recovery of land and later management of the reclaimed site.$$,
$$Reclaiming the Land Beneath the Waste: Transforming India’s Legacy Dumpsites$$,$$https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleseDetailm.aspx?PRID=2313052&lang=1&reg=3$$,$$Press Information Bureau Backgrounder$$,$$2026-09-21$$,
$$["SBM-U 2.0 was launched in October 2021.","Legacy dumpsites are accumulated municipal-waste sites.","The backgrounder cites 62,252 metric tonnes processed and nearly 22 acres reclaimed at Bhalswa.","Dumpsite transformation links waste processing with urban land recovery."]$$::jsonb,
$$[{"question":"What does remediation of a legacy dumpsite aim to achieve?","answer":"Processing accumulated waste and restoring land for safer, productive use."},{"question":"Is one cited city outcome automatically a nationwide completion figure?","answer":"No."}]$$::jsonb,
$${"title":"Legacy-dumpsite transformation","steps":["Waste accumulates at a dumpsite.","Cities process and segregate legacy waste.","Land is reclaimed after remediation.","The reclaimed site is managed for sustainable urban use."]}$$::jsonb,$$published$$,now()
),
(
$$2026-09-22-tumakuru-smart-city-handover$$,$$2026-09-22$$,$$Tumakuru Smart City closes projects and hands assets to city agencies$$,
$$Tumakuru became the first of Karnataka’s seven selected Smart Cities to report full physical and financial project closure. The release says its Special Purpose Vehicle dissolved after operations concluded in October 2025 and assets were handed to the City Corporation and line departments.$$,
$$The update illustrates the Smart Cities Mission’s project-governance model. An SPV can execute projects, but long-term maintenance is handed to regular city institutions; project closure is distinct from launching a new Smart City scheme.$$,
$$The release reports Rs 994 crore expenditure against a Rs 1,000 crore allocation jointly funded by the Union and Karnataka governments. It describes an integrated command and control centre, smart lighting and civic-service systems among implemented interventions.$$,
$$Tumakuru: Karnataka’s First Smart City to Achieve 100% Project Closure$$,$$https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2313059&lang=2&reg=48$$,$$Press Information Bureau Bengaluru$$,$$2026-09-21$$,
$$["Tumakuru is the first of Karnataka’s seven selected Smart Cities to report full closure.","Its Smart City SPV dissolved after operations concluded in October 2025.","Assets were handed to Tumakuru City Corporation and line departments.","The stated funding involved both Union and Karnataka governments."]$$::jsonb,
$$[{"question":"What was handed over after the Tumakuru Smart City SPV closed?","answer":"Development assets were handed to the City Corporation and line departments."},{"question":"Does project closure mean a new Smart City scheme was launched?","answer":"No."}]$$::jsonb,
$${"title":"Smart City project handover","steps":["An SPV plans and executes mission projects.","Assets and digital systems are completed.","The SPV closes after its operational role.","City institutions take long-term maintenance responsibility."]}$$::jsonb,$$published$$,now()
),
(
$$2026-09-22-ayurveda-day-2026-participation$$,$$2026-09-22$$,$$Ayurveda Day 2026 participation dashboard records nationwide activities$$,
$$Ahead of the 11th Ayurveda Day on 23 September, the Ministry of Ayush reported more than 9,700 activities across 30 States and UTs, over 3.6 lakh registered participants and nearly 89.3 lakh citizen pledges through the official microsite.$$,
$$This is a public-health awareness and traditional-medicine outreach update. Participation statistics describe reported engagement, not clinical evidence for a treatment or a regulatory approval for a medicine.$$,
$$The announced theme is “Ayurveda for a Healthier Tomorrow.” The official microsite is used for citizen registration and activity reporting, while activities were also reported from ten countries and territories.$$,
$$Nationwide Public Participation Gathers Momentum Ahead of 11th Ayurveda Day$$,$$https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleseDetailm.aspx?PRID=2312969&lang=1&reg=3$$,$$Ministry of Ayush / Press Information Bureau$$,$$2026-09-21$$,
$$["The 11th Ayurveda Day is observed on 23 September 2026.","Its theme is Ayurveda for a Healthier Tomorrow.","More than 9,700 activities were reported across 30 States and UTs.","The Ayurveda Day microsite supports registration and activity reporting."]$$::jsonb,
$$[{"question":"What is the Ayurveda Day 2026 theme?","answer":"Ayurveda for a Healthier Tomorrow."},{"question":"What is the main function of the official microsite in this release?","answer":"Citizen registration and reporting of activities."}]$$::jsonb,
$${"title":"Public-health awareness campaign","steps":["An official theme and portal are announced.","Institutions register activities.","Citizens participate in outreach and pledges.","Reported engagement is consolidated on the platform."]}$$::jsonb,$$published$$,now()
)
